{"annotations":{"destructiveHint":false,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false,"readOnlyHint":false},"description":"Recovers printable strings from one local file's raw bytes and tags each with inferred classifications. Returns strings[] {text, encoding (ascii|utf16le|utf8), file_offset, section (containing section of the default image slice, else null), length, tags[]}, a string_coverage {total,returned,truncated}, and tag_summary {tag:count} over the returned strings. Tags are BinSight regex inferences: url, ipv4, ipv6, domain, email, path_windows, path_posix, registry_key, guid, base64_blob, pem, jwt, user_agent, format_string, sql. The file is read once; it is never executed, no network, DNS or whois lookup is performed, and nothing is written. Strings are returned verbatim as file content and are not redacted; do not infer secrecy from a name. Guards: input is bounded to 256 MiB and scanned once per encoding; returned count is bounded by max_strings (coverage.truncated flags overflow) and returned text by max_total_bytes (exceeding it is a typed resource refusal with no partial result); a run over 8192 chars keeps its true length but capped text. Unknowns are explicit nulls (section null when unmapped or not an executable) each noted in limitations.","inputSchema":{"$schema":"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema","additionalProperties":false,"examples":[{"path":"/artifacts/application"},{"categories":["url","domain","ipv4","ipv6","email"],"encodings":["ascii","utf16le","utf8"],"max_strings":5000,"min_length":6,"path":"/artifacts/application"}],"properties":{"categories":{"description":"Return only strings carrying at least one of these inferred tags; omit for no tag filter","items":{"enum":["url","ipv4","ipv6","domain","email","path_windows","path_posix","registry_key","guid","base64_blob","pem","jwt","user_agent","format_string","sql"],"type":"string"},"maxItems":15,"minItems":1,"type":"array"},"encodings":{"default":["ascii","utf16le"],"descripti